        "text": "Republican opposition to the ACA created political momentum for Democratic candidates focused on defending it.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Public opinion favors the protection of the Affordable Care Act, making it electorally advantageous.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Strategic messaging around healthcare resonates more effectively than other issues in current electoral politics.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Nancy Pelosi and Democratic leadership possess credible influence over national party strategy.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Electoral success is linked to consistent, high-profile issue framing at the national level.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker assumes the audience recognizes the significance of the ACA in modern U.S. politics.",
