      },
      {
        "text": "Environmental issues encompass multiple dimensions including global climate change, health impacts, tourism dollars, and emerging jobs.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "These topics are complex and interconnected, making them 'fulsome' issues.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Focusing on any single aspect—such as health impact or job creation—does not negate the broader context.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Presenting multiple facets of environmental issues does not require changing the core message but rather expanding its scope.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "When people care about specific aspects like health or jobs, acknowledging those concerns shows engagement with their priorities.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Current public discourse often oversimplifies environmental issues into brief comments that omit important details.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Audiences have diverse values and priorities, and effective communication must acknowledge them.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Complex issues should be communicated through inclusive framing rather than reductionist summaries.",
